# The Rust sources are fingerprinted byte for byte by `make stamp`, and the
# generated file it writes is committed and diffed in CI. A Git for Windows
# checkout defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite both on the way
# out of the object store: the fingerprint would differ from every other
# platform for identical sources, and libstamp.go would never compare equal to
# what the generator writes, so `make lib` would rewrite it on every run and
# leave the tree permanently dirty.
#
# tools/stamp folds CRLF defensively when hashing as well. Keep both: this half
# also keeps the working tree clean, and it only governs checkouts made after it
# lands.
*.rs   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
internal/arti/libstamp.go text eol=lf
